"1 <= head.nodes <= 500","-500 <= Node.val <= 500","1 <= left <= right","right <= head.nodes"],"hints":["Find the node just before position left. A dummy head handles left = 1.","Reverse the next (right − left + 1) nodes the usual way, remembering the node where the reversed part starts (it becomes its tail).","Reconnect: the node before the section points to the new section head, and the old section head points to the node after the section. Or repeatedly move the next node to the front of the section."],"explain":"Positions 2 to 4 hold 2, 3, 4. Reversing only that part gives 4, 3, 2 while 1 and 5 stay in place: `[1,4,3,2,5]`."},
